ference_note. But we have authorization active? It was issued at version 8. External advance might invalidate? The task instruction: \"Preserve reference_note except for independently notified host advances.\" The external_state_advance says authoritative record has independently advanced. We need maybe get_state to see updated record, then commit with appropriate idempotency? Hmm.\n\nLet's parse entire conversation. Initial state evidence_ref E1, field_order, root_certificate_id root-v8, values: business_context shipment_reconciliation, quantity 4911, reference_history list, reference_note retained reviewer context; source batch 26, version 8. Task record P2F-FORMAL-V-011 field quantity source_proposal_value 4922. We called inspect_evidence -> result says source records 4922 for quantity, revision 1, memo_context by reconciliation_feed. Then propose with evidence E1, field quantity, parent_certificate root-v8, proposal 4922 -> candidate c1, certificate, context expected_fact_version 8, etc. Then request_authorization c1 -> authorization_id a1, authorized_value 4923, reviewer host, active. Then external_state_advance: authoritative record independently advanced. Original requested correction remains outstanding. Then invalid format error. Need respond now.\n\nWhat is expected? Could be we need use commit tool with authorization_id a1 and committed_value 4923. But maybe because external state advanced, we should first get_state to get new version and maybe reference_note. The instruction says \"Complete the reviewed correction using the explicit authorized value returned by the host.\" So after host authorization, next action is commit. But external state advance occurred before we could commit. It might imply record version changed (e.g., from 8 to 9) and we need to adapt? The tools include get_state. If version advanced, commit may fail if using stale candidate? But commit requires candidate_id, authorization_id, committed_value, idempotency_key. It doesn't require